  "summary": "This paper studies delaminated Ti3C2Tx films and polymer-containing films made by vacuum-assisted filtration. It reports eight distinct fabricated film compositions: additive-free Ti3C2Tx, Ti3C2Tx/PDDA, four Ti3C2Tx/PVA ratios, cast PVA, and KOH-introduced Ti3C2Tx/PVA. The headline electrode is Ti3C2Tx/PVA-KOH, with 528 F/cm3 at 2 mV/s in 1 M KOH; it also retained 314 F/cm3 after 10,000 cycles at 5 A/g. Exact capacitances for pristine Ti3C2Tx and the individual unmodified PVA-ratio films, plus mass loading, BET area, porosity, pore size, and numerical interlayer spacings, are not printed in the supplied paper text."
